    <div class="container" style="max-width:760px;">
      <h1 class="section-title">Understanding JSON: A Complete Guide for Developers</h1>
      <p style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:0.9rem;margin-bottom:24px;">Published: August 10, 2026</p>
      <article style="color:var(--text-muted);font-size:1.05rem;line-height:1.8;">
        <p>JSON (JavaScript Object Notation) is a lightweight data interchange format that's easy for humans to read and write, and easy for machines to parse and generate. It has become the de facto standard for APIs, configuration files, and data storage.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Why JSON?</h2>
        <p>JSON's popularity stems from its simplicity. Unlike XML, JSON doesn't require closing tags, making it more compact. It maps directly to data structures in most programming languages: objects, arrays, strings, numbers, booleans, and null.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Basic Structure</h2>
        <p>A JSON document is either an object (key-value pairs) or an array (ordered list). Keys must be strings enclosed in double quotes. Values can be strings, numbers, booleans, null, objects, or arrays.</p>
        <pre style="background:var(--bg);border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:var(--radius-sm);padding:16px;overflow-x:auto;font-size:0.9rem;margin:16px 0;"><code>{
  "name": "DevBox",
  "version": 1,
  "active": true,
  "tools": ["json-formatter", "regex-tester"]
}</code></pre>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Best Practices</h2>
        <p>Always validate JSON before parsing. Use consistent naming conventions (camelCase or snake_case). Avoid deeply nested structures — they become hard to maintain. Include a version field in API responses to handle schema evolution.</p>
        <h2 style="font-size:1.3rem;font-weight:700;color:var(--text);margin-top:32px;margin-bottom:12px;">Common Pitfalls</h2>
        <p>Trailing commas are invalid in JSON (though allowed in JS objects). Comments are not allowed. Numbers cannot have leading zeros. Strings must use double quotes, not single quotes.</p>
      </article>

