      <section class="faq" style="margin-top:32px;">
        <h3>Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
        <details>
          <summary>Is JSON a programming language?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">No. JSON is a data format, not a programming language. It has no variables, loops, or functions.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What's the difference between JSON and JavaScript objects?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">JSON is a text representation. JavaScript objects are in-memory data structures. JSON.stringify() converts JS objects to JSON; JSON.parse() converts JSON to JS objects.</div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Can JSON represent dates?</summary>
          <div class="faq-body">JSON has no native date type. Dates are typically represented as ISO 8601 strings (e.g., "2026-08-14T00:00:00Z").</div>
        </details>
      </section>
